node/
WatcherBrain/node/
*.log
*.zip
Watcher.zip
blocked-requests.log
watchdog_loop.pid
last_spool_cleanup_day.txt
# Per-machine "hardening last re-asserted at" clock (mtime only). Runtime state, so it
# must never commit or ship in the bundle. Harmless if it did (an old mtime just means
# "due now"), but keep the folder clean. See poll-hub.js reassertHardeningIfDue.
WatcherBrain/harden-last.txt

# Fleet dashboard secrets/state — never committed. HubConfig.json holds the
# enrollment secret (repo is PUBLIC); hub-credential.json is the per-machine
# credential issued back on registration. See WatcherBrain/HubConfig.example.json.
WatcherBrain/HubConfig.json
WatcherBrain/hub-credential.json
# Transient plaintext master code (written at repo root by AskIdentity.ps1,
# scrubbed by the installer after enroll) and the per-machine salted uninstall
# hash (in WatcherBrain). Bare names so they match wherever they land. Neither
# must ever be committed.
master-code.plain
uninstall-code.hash
WatcherBrain/unplugged.flag
WatcherBrain/whitelist-version.txt
WatcherBrain/poll-log-cursor.txt
# Per-machine chosen proxy port (written at install by proxy-port.js select).
WatcherBrain/proxy-port.txt
# Per-machine last register-with-hub.js outcome (ok/already_enrolled/bad_code/...),
# read by WinConfigWizard.ps1 to show a specific result screen. Not secret.
WatcherBrain/register-status.txt
WatcherBrain/update.log
# Failed-version cooldown marker (self-update.js writes it on a rolled-back update;
# poll-hub.js honors it). Runtime-only per-machine state — must never be committed
# or shipped in the /descargar bundle (would block a fresh install's first update).
WatcherBrain/update-failed.json
# Plan 0003 staging gate — per-machine runtime state. CRITICAL that these never commit AND never ship:
# the bundle's exclude mechanism is .gitignore-driven, and a stray staging.flag in a fresh install would
# mark EVERY new machine as staging → running real cutover cycles on real bancas.
WatcherBrain/staging.flag
WatcherBrain/selftest-state.json
WatcherBrain/selftest.lock
WatcherBrain/_backup_*/
# Plan 0011 "Settings vigilados" — per-machine runtime marker poll-hub.js writes after a
# guard re-check confirms everything OK. Runtime state, never commit or ship in the bundle.
WatcherBrain/guards-ok.txt
# Plan 0012 — per-machine "hibernate has been forced here at least once" marker written by
# HardenPower.ps1. CRITICAL that it never ships in the bundle: a fresh install carrying a
# stray flag would arrive pre-baselined and swallow its FIRST real hibernate revert as
# housekeeping instead of reporting it as tamper.
WatcherBrain/hibernate-baselined.flag
# Plan 0013 — per-machine "this machine has enabled the print log at least once" marker,
# written by HardenPrinters.ps1. Same reason as the one above: a stray flag in a fresh
# install would arrive pre-baselined and read its FIRST real revert as housekeeping.
WatcherBrain/print-log-baselined.flag
WatcherBrain/location-baselined.flag
# Plan 0018 — per-machine geo-IP fallback cache (last public-IP location), refreshed
# ~every few hours on the box. Runtime state: never commit it, and (bundle EXCLUDE is
# .gitignore-driven) never let a dev cache ship into a fresh install and seed the fleet.
WatcherBrain/geoip.json
WatcherBrain/geoip-attempt.txt
# Plan 0019 — per-machine location-off state machine: the mutable no-fix counter and the
# set-once "armed" (≥2 real fixes seen) flag. Runtime state: never commit AND never ship a
# dev copy into a fresh install (a pre-armed/pre-counted flag would mis-fire the alert).
WatcherBrain/location-state.json
WatcherBrain/location-armed.flag
# Plan 0013 — per-machine harvest cursor (last EventRecordID of PrintService/Operational
# already posted to the hub), owned exclusively by poll-hub.js. Never commit AND never ship:
# a shipped copy would arrive with the installed files' +h +s attributes, where Node's
# writeFileSync (CREATE_ALWAYS) throws EPERM — freezing the cursor at the shipped value, so
# the harvest would die silently and every banca would read "sin impresión" forever.
WatcherBrain/print-cursor.txt
# Plan 0013 — "the harvest failure is already reported" marker, so a permanent failure costs one
# line in the shared events.log instead of 720 a day (that log is capped AND is what diagnostics
# uploads). Runtime state; must never commit or ship.
WatcherBrain/print-harvest-failed.flag
# v1.0.38 launcher rename — per-machine "the Install/Uninstall reconciliation already ran here"
# marker, written by poll-hub.js (reconcileLaunchers) once the swap is complete. Glob so future
# launcher migrations (launchers-1.0.NN.done) are covered too. CRITICAL that these never commit
# AND never ship: the bundle/OTA exclude mechanism is .gitignore-driven, and a stray marker in a
# release would make every machine's first post-update poll return early — leaving the obsolete
# launchers in place and the new Install.exe/Uninstall.exe VISIBLE (the exact disguise leak this
# migration exists to close).
WatcherBrain/launchers-*.done

# Local Claude Code project state (agent worktrees, per-session config) — local-only tooling,
# never part of the repo or the /descargar bundle. Ignoring it keeps `git status` clean and
# prevents the leftover "embedded git repository" worktrees from ever being committed.
.claude/
